Here's a little situation that I came across that I thought was very
interesting:

I was a level 9 or so Valkyrie, and had discovered a chaotic altar.
There was also a soldiers barracks on that same level.  Feeling like
my chaotic self, I sacrificed every human corpse I could find, and got
some wild results.  

	I obviously summoned all sorts of demons.  Yeenogho, Jubilex, pit
fiends, balrog, vrocks, subbuci, etc.  (In case anyone doesn't know, they
are friendly and do not attack you (exception- see below!)) After
many sacrifices, and several artifacts later, I got bold, and started 
killing demons.  Jubilex, vrock, pit fiends, subbuci, they all went down.
I was still sacrificing everything I could.  A voice had announced
"You are destined to take lives for (God's name)" or something like that.
I discovered a neat meaning to this- I was fighting balrog, and he nailed
me pretty bad with two hits.  I prayed, and watched my health scroll
about three times from maximum to zero.  I finished off balrog- although it
seems like I died three times in the process!  

	This was the best game I had had... I had gotten to the maze levels,
and hit a teleport trap.  Having control, I decided to go back to 8, and
work down, because I still needed a few things.  By this time I was level
15.  On the way down, I passed the altar level again, and one demon still
remained:  Yeenogho.  I figured I could take him, because everything else
was falling so easily.....    he finished me with two hits.   AAaaaargh!!

	moral:  Don't attack Yeenogho without magic resistance!!! 

	And although I'm unsure of this, in a different game, he attacked
me when I was hallucinating- I didn't provoke him.  Beware!



